    "lawCode": "Amd §8-400, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A7347                REVISED 6/10/09\n\nTITLE  OF BILL:  An act to amend the election law, in relation to making\napplications for absentee ballots\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: To change the absentee  ballot  process\nby  allowing  qualified  voters  to  request an absentee ballot from the\nBoard of Elections by letter, telefax or other written instrument.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:  Section 1, Paragraph (d) of subdivision\n2 of section 8-400 of the Election Law is amended by  permitting  quali-\nfied  voters  to request and absentee ballot from the board of elections\nin writing in letter, telefax or other written instrument.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: Currently, requests by qualified voters are only accepta-\nble in letter. This legislation would  add  telefax  and  other  written\ninstruments as additional ways in which the requests may be made.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nA. 4490-A and S. 4960 of 2007/2008\nA. 7980 of 2005/2006\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect on the first of January next\nsucceeding  the date on which it shall have become a law and shall apply\nto all elections or primaries conducted on or after such date. Effective\nimmediately the addition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule  or  regu-\nlation  necessary  for  the  implementation of this act on its effective\ndate are authorized and directed to be made and completed on  or  before\nsuch effective date.\n\n",
