    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A7347A               REVISED 1/20/10\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:    An  act  to amend the election law, in relation to\nmaking applications for absentee ballots\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: To change the absentee ballot process\nby allowing qualified voters to request an absentee  ballot  from  the\nBoard of Elections by letter, telefax or other written instrument.\n\nSUMMARY   OF   SPECIFIC   PROVISIONS:  Section  1,  Paragraph  (d)  of\nsubdivision 2 of section 8-400 of  the  Election  Law  is  amended  by\npermitting  qualified  voters  to request and absentee ballot from the\nboard of elections in writing in  letter,  telefax  or  other  written\ninstrument.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  Currently,  requests  by  qualified  voters  are  only\nacceptable in letter, This legislation would  add  telefax  and  other\nwritten  instruments  as  additional ways in which the requests may be\nmade.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  A. 4490-A and S. 4960 of 2007/2008 A. 7980\nof 2005/2006\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect on  the  first  of  January\nnext  succeeding  the  date  on  which it shall have become a law and.\nshall apply to all elections or primaries conducted on or  after  such\ndate.  Effective  immediately the addition, amendment and/or repeal of\nany rule or regulation necessary for the implementation of this act on\nits effective  date  are  authorized  and  directed  to  be  made  and\ncompleted on or before such effective date.\n\n",
